"""Score and spray settings behind every saved stream result, from a code audit of all 51 scoring scripts (2026-10-17).

Each entry maps output path patterns (fnmatch, repository-relative) to the script that writes them and to what it computes:
  score: "wrapper" = grid4_common.score (version set by the write date: S2 / S3 / S4-pooled, see VERSIONS in
         score_provenance.py), or a fixed version when the script calls the score functions directly
         ("S2 direct" = score_conditional with its own defaults: legacy chi bins, implied background boxes; "S0" = score;
         "S1" / "S1 robust" = score_chi_kde with robust False / True; "S2 re-implemented" = obs_split.single_scores or a
         plotting re-implementation of the S2 model);
  options: every non-default score option (empty = none);
  spray: particle / spray settings of the scored models (make_spray defaults unless stated: nrel 8000, seed 1,
         PMs (-3.2223, -6.7517), frame baumgardt, uniform release over the last 1000 Myr, trailing arm, no age cut);
  recorded: which of these the output itself stores.
Used by score_provenance.py to fill the results index. New scripts should save grid4_common.score(...)["settings"] instead.
"""

